\name{cellucid_history_anndata_save}
\alias{cellucid_history_anndata_save}
\title{Save AnnData with this state}
\usage{
cellucid_history_anndata_save(viewer, file)
}
\arguments{
\item{viewer}{A viewer \code{\link{cellucid_view}()} or \code{\link{cellucid_serve}()} returned.}
\item{file}{The new file's name (.zarr.zip is added when it does not end so); "<dataset> with this state.zarr.zip" when left out. Text (at least 1 character). Left out unless given (the viewer then chooses as its own control does).}
}
\value{
A \code{cellucid_action_request}, at once and invisibly: the action is sent now, or when the viewer's channel opens.
\code{\link{cellucid_action_result}(request)} returns its outcome: a list of \code{applied} (False when every change was in the dataset already (no record added)), \code{branch}, \code{bytes}, \code{cells} (Cells written: every cell of the dataset, whichever were open), \code{file} (The file's name), \code{layout} (A Cellucid-ready AnnData, or a MuData for a dataset of several modalities), \code{left_out} (What the copy does not hold of the state, or of the dataset, one sentence each), \code{rows} (Every change of the apply plan, in domain order, as Python and R plan it), \code{step} (The step applied: the one shown), \code{to} (file: a file the person chose in the save dialog; download: the browser's downloads), \code{tracker}.
}
\description{
Write a new Cellucid-ready AnnData file (.zarr.zip) of the whole open dataset with the state shown applied, as Python and R apply a session: renamed labels, user-defined fields and highlight groups as obs columns, gene sets in uns and var, and a record of what was applied; never over the dataset's own file.
}
\details{
The viewer's action \code{history.anndata.save} (History). It acts outside the viewer's state and history (a file the person receives in the browser, a publication, or what the browser keeps for later visits), which Undo does not take back: it makes no step of the history.

When an agent (Claude, ChatGPT) runs it, the viewer asks the person first (writes-file); from R it is not asked.
}
\seealso{
\code{\link{cellucid_act}()} sends any action by its type, and \code{\link{cellucid_action_result}()}
collects its answer.
}
\examples{
if (interactive() && requireNamespace("SeuratObject", quietly = TRUE)) {
  data("pbmc_small", package = "SeuratObject")
  viewer <- cellucid_view(SeuratObject::UpdateSeuratObject(pbmc_small))
  request <- cellucid_history_anndata_save(viewer)
  print(request)
  # cellucid_action_result(request) waits for its outcome.
  cellucid_stop(viewer)
}
}
